msgid "The -v form usually says what the noun is doing now. Usually you take the he, she form of the verb and change -b to -v: <0>magab</0> gives <1>magav</1>, so <2/> is a child who is asleep, and <3/> is water that is running."
msgstr "The -v form usually says what the noun is doing now. Usually you take the he, she form of the verb and change -b to -v: <0>magab</0> gives <1>magav</1>, so <2/> is a child who is asleep, and <3/> is water that is running."

msgid "The <0>-ma</0> of the verb usually becomes -nud: <1>väsima</1> gives <2>väsinud</2>. Some verbs shorten or change: <3>tulema</3> gives <4>tulnud</4>."
msgstr "The <0>-ma</0> of the verb usually becomes -nud: <1>väsima</1> gives <2>väsinud</2>. Some verbs shorten or change: <3>tulema</3> gives <4>tulnud</4>."

